# Collision & Layers

From assignment PDF **Must: Collision** — these are not optional for submission.

## Push (crate)

- At least one landing platform blocked by a crate; walking into it moves it
- Real physical object: mass, friction; shove off edge; push onto ice and keep going; stand on it and jump from it
- Must never clip inside walls/floor; must never push the player through geometry
- If using CharacterController, document how pushing works (it does not come for free)

## Get shot

- At least one enemy fires a projectile
- Hit does **not** cost a life — knockback impulse absorbed and decayed without losing control
- Must compose with: airborne, ice, moving platform, leaning on crate
- Knocked off a ledge is a legitimate death

## Collision hygiene

- Projectiles must not tunnel through platforms or player at full speed
- Projectiles must not hit the firing enemy or other projectiles
- Implement via **layer collision matrix** + appropriate collision detection mode
- **Not** via tag comparisons inside `OnTriggerEnter`
- Document layer layout in **README**

## Stomp vs hit (related)

- Stomp from above: enemy dies, player bounces (holding jump = higher bounce)
- Side or below contact: player takes the hit (costs a life)
- Discrimination must hold at full falling speed and 30 fps
